A||||14||MooCow||Duster vs. Fiero?  + Another question ||||5||
Z||000000||MooCow||03-08-2000||10:19 PM||||Okay First which is faster a stock Fiero with a v6 any year, or a stock v6 Plymouth Duster like a 93.  At cars.com they say the Duster has 141 horse power @5200 RPM and Torque is rated 171 @ 2400 RMP.  Also it only weighs in at 2617lbs.  Isn't that lighter with more torque and more horsepower than a v6 Fiero??<P>Next question I have is what should I do?<BR>This guy owns an 86SE v6 Fiero gold and I believe he had it for sale last summer. All I know is it has just been sitting there all winter and its like summer here in Muskegon, Michigain so he should go drive it. I was wondering if I should just go knock on his door and ask the guy if it is for sale or not.  Would any of you guys/gals be mad if a 18 year old came to your house asking if you are selling your Fiero cause it has just been sitting there??<BR>All info on both matters will help out greatly.  Thanks                  Ken<P>[This message has been edited by MooCow (edited 03-08-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by MooCow (edited 03-08-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Shiner||03-08-2000||10:32 PM||||It's almost a given.  Everytime I see a fiero that has been sitting in one place for awhile I start talking to people.  Almost every damn one I asked about could be purchased.  Go up and talk to the guy.  At least you might get an intresting story out of it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||william_thorniii||03-08-2000||10:48 PM||||MooCow,<P>Go for it.  I definitely wouldn't get mad.  Hey you might even get a great deal if the wife wants it gone (or something like that).  <P>...and... <P>sadly the Duster does stack up better on paper.  I do not partake in street racing, so I cannot vouch for either car in real world situations.  <P>William T. Thorn, III<p>[This message has been edited by william_thorniii (edited 03-08-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000003||RICK||03-08-2000||11:29 PM||||MooCow, those were my two cars until the Duster decided to go backwards at 60mph into a wall (that's another story) the Fiero is better, I think, as far as speed, handling, and looks.  The Duster was more comfortable to ride in, but I'm a big guy.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||03-09-2000||04:58 AM||||Definitely stop and ask about the car.  The worst the owner can do is tell you to get the heck off of his property.  What have you lost?  Remember to give the owner a Forum card.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcard_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||MooCow||03-09-2000||08:49 AM||||Everyone thanks for the responses so far. I have a choice to get a Fiero if the guy is going to sell it if not I may buy that Duster.  Today after school I'm going to ask the guy if he is selling the Fiero and I will give him that card.  Thanks Ken||||reg||10
Z||000006||ChadMan||03-09-2000||09:14 AM||||Aw, MooCow, buy a Fiero!  There's so much more to consider here than just straight-line acceleration, which would be very, very close between a V6 Duster and a stock V6 Fiero.<P>IMHO...<BR>1) FWD performance cars don't handle as well as RWD performance cars.<BR>2) The only reliable Chrysler automobiles made after 1981 were rebadged Mitsubishis.<BR>3) Metal cars rust.<BR>4) There are plenty of performance upgrades available for the 2.8 V6 - not sure about the 3.0 in the Duster.<BR>5) All Fieros look cool.  The Duster looks like a rebodied K-car (which, of course, it is).<BR>6) The Fiero has no back seat - so your friends will never make you drive when you're all going out to the bars.<BR>7) There is no Duster forum!!!<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000007||mwbackus||03-09-2000||11:01 AM||||And the number 1 reason not to buy a Duster:<P>The speed governor is nearly impossible to defeat, and limits you to a unrespectable 100 mph.  (Hence the Fiero is most definatly "faster").<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000008||william_thorniii||03-09-2000||11:48 AM||||MooCow,<P>You cheated!  You didn't ask which was a better car.  I stand by my previous decision that a Duster is quicker in a straight line... but it is DEFINITELY not a better car.  I have owned Chrysler products in the past and unless DC really gets going in a different direction, never will again.  Fiero's are a much more fun all around car.  Not to mention faster through the corners.  <P>Can you imagine the excitement in a Duster forum?  I bet they hate Tom and Ray (The Car Guys), they always seem to be ripping on the Dodge Dart/Plymouth Duster of yesteryear.  <P>Go with a Fiero... even if you have to wait to find the right one. <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000009||HF6582||03-09-2000||02:05 PM||||Don't buy the Duster!!!!!  The 3.0L is JUNK!!<BR>I drive a Dodge Spirt to work with the 3.0 and it is not a very good motor. cam bearing rattle on start up lifters bleed off after setting for awhile (get the annoying lifter tick)<P>Most Dodge cars are put together poorly.<P>Change oil every 3000, so this motor should NOT have any problems.<P>3.0L very hard on valve stem seals.<P>I cound go on all day long if you want.<P>Scott  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||13
Z||000010||Raydar||03-09-2000||04:04 PM||||Is the 3.0 V-6 the same motor that's in all those Dodge Caravans that I see driving down the road, being followed by the huge clouds of burnt oil smoke? <BR>I haven't seen anything burn that much oil since before all the Chevy Vegas were reclaimed by oxidation.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||03-09-2000||04:16 PM||||I was driving on the highway a couple of weeks ago, and what looked like an 85 Duster (a friend has one of those, and I've seen photos of it) screamed past when I was turning onto the highway.. I stepped on it, but couldn't catch it.. I didn't go over 120kph as it was raining and well.. a ford taurus isn't a sports car.. but either way, I couldn't catch it. I saw that it had a "turbo" badge on the back, but I didn't see what kind of car it was.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Eric||03-09-2000||08:22 PM||||My friend's Dodge Shadow can pull away from my modified 88 GT 3.1.  That car is pretty fast; it can chirp the tires from the first to second and second to third gear shifts and that's with ~400lbs of people in there.  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Standard||03-10-2000||01:13 AM||||a while ago there was a thread about the mopar sleepers, i think.  i hate those things.. on of my first stoplight races with the GT was against a guy in some '80s dodge, don't know what type.  small boxy thing.  it was a 2 lane street that turned to 1 lane about 500 feet after the intersection.  didn't get a good launch, but we were even all the way up to were it narrowed down.  I think he let off 'cause I just wouldn't let him in my lane.. oops  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||11
Z||000014||william_thorniii||03-10-2000||07:33 PM||||The worst of the worst are the Shelby tuned Omni's.  The damn things are being towed more often than they are running, but when they are running... you had better WATCH OUT!<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||4
